      "id": "6eob06d",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Factors Affecting Climate of India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "India's climate is governed by geographical factors including latitude, altitude, relief, and monsoon winds.",
        "The South-West Monsoon advances through two distinct branches: the Arabian Sea Branch and the Bay of Bengal Branch.",
        "Local weather patterns before the monsoon are influenced by regional pre-monsoon winds like Loo and Kalbaisakhi.",
        "Global oceanic-atmospheric phenomena such as El Niño and La Niña significantly affect Indian monsoon rainfall variation."
      ],
      "id": "wd4x9qg"
